// CDLGAPSIDESIDEWHITE recognizes the Up/Down-gap side-by-side white lines
// pattern over bars startIdx through endIdx.
//
// A three-candle pattern: a first candle followed by two white candles of
// similar body size that both gap the same direction (up or down) from the
// first candle's real body and open at about the same level. It is a
// continuation signal whose sign reports the gap direction; the code does not
// verify a prior trend.
//
// Formula and more info at https://ta-lib.org/functions/cdlgapsidesidewhite.
//
// Inputs, each at least endIdx+1 long:
//   - inOpen: Open price of each bar.
//   - inHigh: High price of each bar.
//   - inLow: Low price of each bar.
//   - inClose: Close price of each bar.
//
// Outputs, each at least as long as the values written (the input length always
// suffices):
//   - outInteger: +100 for an up-gap (bullish continuation), -100 for a
//     down-gap (bearish continuation), 0 when no pattern. Sign is set solely by
//     the C2-vs-C1 gap direction (realbodygapup ? 100 : -100)
//
